  "result": "Excellent! All 164 tests pass. Here's a summary of the payment terms implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\n\u2705 **Added payment terms support to `createInvoice`:**\n- Accepts optional `terms` parameter: `'NET14'`, `'NET30'` (default), or `'EOM'`\n- Calculates and sets `invoice.dueDate` based on terms:\n  - **NET14**: 14 days after issue date\n  - **NET30**: 30 days after issue date (default)\n  - **EOM**: Last day of the month of the issue date (with leap year support)\n- Returns error `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown terms\n\n\u2705 **Preserved terms and dueDate across all invoice operations:**\n- `addLine()` preserves terms and dueDate when modifying draft invoices\n- `removeLine()` preserves terms and dueDate when modifying draft invoices\n- `issueInvoice()` preserves terms and dueDate when issuing\n- `recordPayment()` preserves terms and dueDate when recording payments\n\n\u2705 **Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code** to `src/errors.js`\n\n\u2705 **Added 11 comprehensive tests** to `test/invoices.test.js`:\n- Default NET30 terms applied\n- NET14, NET30, and EOM terms calculation\n- EOM with 28-day February\n- EOM with leap year (29-day February)\n- Error handling for invalid terms\n- Terms preservation through addLine, removeLine, and issueInvoice\n\nAll 164 tests pass.",
